# Cursor rules for Bring It Home

## App identity
Name: Bring It Home
Tagline: Every team starts the tournament. Only one nation brings it home.
Tournament: FIFA World Cup 2026 — USA, Canada, Mexico. 48 teams, 104 matches.

## Brand voice
- Bold, editorial, emotional. Like a great sports broadcaster.
- Short sentences. Present tense. Make the user feel the stakes.
- Never corporate. Never bland. Every line of copy should feel alive.
- The word "home" carries meaning — lean into it where natural.

## Tone examples
  Good: "Every team starts the tournament. Only one brings it home."
  Good: "Japan have done it again. The bracket is in chaos."
  Bad:  "View match statistics and prediction data for your selected teams."

## Stack
Next.js 14 App Router · TypeScript · Tailwind CSS · Zustand · SWR · Google Gemini SDK

## File conventions
- Pages:      src/app/[route]/page.tsx
- Components: src/components/[feature]/ComponentName.tsx  (PascalCase)
- Hooks:      src/hooks/useHookName.ts
- API routes: src/app/api/[route]/route.ts
- Types:      src/types/index.ts  (single source of truth)
- State:      src/lib/store.ts    (Zustand, persisted to localStorage)
- Mock data:  src/lib/data.ts

## Styling
- Tailwind only — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- Utility classes: .card, .btn, .btn-primary, .badge-* from globals.css
- Colours: blue #185FA5, green #3B6D11, amber #854F0B, red #A32D2D
- Cards: bg-white border border-gray-100 rounded-xl p-4
- Spacing: gap-4, p-4, rounded-xl for cards — be consistent

## Key patterns
- API routes auto-fallback to mock data when the relevant API key is missing
- API-Football calls → src/lib/api-football.ts only (never direct from components)
- Weather calls → src/lib/weather.ts
- AI/Gemini calls → src/lib/gemini.ts (server-side ONLY — never in client components)
- Bracket state → useBracketStore (pickWinner, resetBracket, getBracketShareUrl)
- Predictions + streak → usePredictionStore
- SWR hooks poll /api/matches every 30s for live scores

## Build order (what to build next)
1. src/components/bracket/BracketSimulator.tsx
   → Full R32→Final bracket. Click team name/flag/stadium for info panels.
   → Advance button picks winner. Share bracket via getBracketShareUrl().
   → Uses useBracketStore from store.ts.

2. src/components/players/PlayerCard.tsx + PlayerGrid.tsx
   → FIFA-style card: PAC SHO PAS DRI DEF PHY attributes.
   → Click to expand: heatmap, WC stats, form tracker, tactical analysis button.
   → Filter by position, search by name/team.

3. src/components/groups/IfThisHappens.tsx
   → Toggle match results (Team A win / Draw / Team B win).
   → Standings table recalculates live. Qualification probability bars.
   → "What this means" insight panel updates automatically.

4. src/components/timeline/TournamentTimeline.tsx
   → Horizontal day rail. Each day = a story chapter.
   → Player of the day, match results, community mood vote, streak bar.
   → Future days locked until matches are played.

5. src/components/wrapped/WCWrapped.tsx
   → End-of-matchday personalised stats card.
   → Correct predictions, scorers called, accuracy rank, favourite team.
   → Shareable image via html2canvas or server-side OG image.

6. src/components/ui/StreakBar.tsx
   → Global persistent streak counter. Shown on every page.
   → Days active, correct picks, fan IQ level badge.

## API keys (copy .env.local.example → .env.local)
- FOOTBALL_API_KEY   → api-football.com (free: 100 req/day)
- WEATHER_API_KEY    → openweathermap.org (free: 1000 req/day)
- GEMINI_API_KEY     → aistudio.google.com/apikey

## Deploy
vercel --prod  (zero config for Next.js 14)
Set all env vars in Vercel dashboard → Settings → Environment Variables
